Same as floating eyes being a color that blends well into the background
making them easy to ignore if you play in a hurry but also easy to see
if you play slowly (play fast, type slowly).

> At least some of the color confusion does seem to be intentional:
> consider the otherwise completely inexplicable Elvenking on the Plane
> of Earth.

Elven kings come with a pick axe.  To a player who had no idea what to
expect after exiting the dungeon carrying the Amultet it gives them the
ability to eventually escape that level even if they have no other
method of digging - The tool is there on the level and it will
eventually reach their location.

> An interesting detail is that, while dwarf kings and mind flayers have
> been the same color in all versions that had both, the colors are not
> written the same way in the source: dwarf kings are HI_LORD, while
> mind flayers are simply CLR_MAGENTA.  Both map to the same actual
> color, though.

So it is ambiguous if the color overlap was a deliberate feature.  I've
killed dwarf kings in hails of missiles just in case.


